From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:44:25 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] metrics: P2P handshakes, pings, address tables, bans
 and misbehavior

The P2P metrics counted peers and traffic, but not the health of the
connections: how long handshakes and pings take, how full the address
tables are, and who is being banned, discouraged or caught misbehaving.

- The transport label now distinguishes WebSocket over TLS: tcp, ws,
  wss (was tcp, websocket), on fullnode_peers,
  fullnode_p2p_connections_total and the new series below. The migration
  table says so.
- fullnode_p2p_handshake_seconds{direction,transport}: from the CNode's
  creation (a steady clock read there when metrics are on) to its verack.
  Outbound WebSocket peers are dialled, TLS-negotiated and upgraded
  before their CNode exists, so that part is not included.
- fullnode_p2p_ping_seconds{transport}: the round trip PONG handling
  already computes.
- fullnode_addrman_addresses{table=new|tried}: AddrMan::NewTriedCounts,
  new, read at scrape time (addrman's mutex, briefly).
- fullnode_p2p_bans_total (BanMan::Ban) and fullnode_p2p_banned_subnets
  (the ban list's size at scrape time, as listbanned reads it).
- fullnode_p2p_discouragements_total{outcome=discouraged|
  disconnected_local|exempt_noban|exempt_manual}: each branch of
  MaybeDiscourageAndDisconnect.
- fullnode_p2p_misbehavior_total{reason}: Misbehaving() takes free text,
  some of it formatted. A fixed set of ten reason classes (handshake,
  oversized_message, invalid_header, invalid_block,
  invalid_compact_block, invalid_tx, bloom_filter, avalanche,
  avalanche_proof, other) is assigned by ClassifyMisbehavior from the
  fixed messages net_processing uses (each one unit-tested), or given
  explicitly where the message is a validation result's reject reason
  (MaybePunishNodeForBlock: invalid_block or invalid_header by result;
  MaybePunishNodeForTx: invalid_tx; proof registration: avalanche_proof).

Cardinality: handshake 6 label sets, ping 3, addrman 2, bans 1, banned
1, discouragements 4, misbehavior 10; peers grows from 32 to 48 series
and connections from 4 to 6.

Hot paths: one steady clock read per new connection and one ring push
per handshake and per pong; misbehavior and discouragement are rare. No
lock is added to message handling.

Evidence:
- metrics_tests/misbehavior_reasons (every fixed message's class),
  addrman_tests (new: new/tried counts after Add and Good), banman_tests,
  denialofservice_tests, net_tests pass.
- interface_metrics_p2p.py: six handshake label sets; the two nodes'
  handshakes are timed over tcp; a P2P peer adds one inbound tcp
  handshake and pings are timed; addpeeraddress moves new and tried by
  one each; setban counts a ban and one banned subnet, clearbanned
  empties it; an oversized inv counts one oversized_message misbehavior
  and, the peer being local, one disconnected_local.
- interface_http_metrics.py: the WebSocket peer is counted under
  transport="ws" and its handshake is timed.

Not tested: wss peers (covered by the same index from the TLS flag);
discouragement of non-local peers and the noban/manual exemptions.
